      "subject": "Chemistry",
      "question": "Why does increasing temperature speed up a reaction? I want a collision-theory answer I can use in a 3-mark question.",
      "status": "Resolved",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T09:20:00",
      "answers": [
        {
          "id": "a4",
          "author_id": "u6",
          "author_name": "Mr. Rao",
          "explanation": "Higher temperature means particles move faster and collide more often. A larger fraction of collisions also reach the activation energy, so more collisions are successful and the reaction speeds up.",
